# Rule 3/5 (absence engine). A GitHub Actions workflow with no top-level
# `permissions:` block runs with the repo's default (often write-all) token
# scope — violating least privilege. Flag a workflow file where `permissions:`
# never appears. content_contains gates it to real workflow files.
id: KEUR-CICD-003
maturity: 2
title: Workflow has no permissions block (least-privilege token scope)
category: sast
severity: warning
engine: absence
action: warn
target:
  extensions: .yml .yaml
  content_contains: "on:"
patterns:
  - regex: (?im)^\s*permissions\s*:
    message: "This workflow declares no `permissions:` block, so it uses the default (often write-all) GITHUB_TOKEN scope. Add a least-privilege permissions: block (e.g. contents: read)."
confidence: 0.5
fix: "Add a top-level `permissions:` block scoped to the minimum the workflow needs (start from contents: read)."
